  "definitions": "Warm priming is excluded; all cells pass cache-hit accounting, one-output-token and no-preemption checks. GPU-only resident cells require every expected prefix token in GPU cache, with zero CPU offload loads. CPU cells reset GPU cache after priming and verify CPU restoration. Full-resident references fit the unchanged GPU KV pool. Capacity-limited 75-request 60K episodes explicitly permit prefix misses and are not an all-hits ceiling. Throughput is the mean of episode rates; aggregate throughput is also given. Tail TTFT here is pooled across measured requests. CPU and GPU cache modes use independent allocations. GPU-only uses ordinary worker preparation without the connector-dependent observer or scheduler holds, so this is a measured resident reference, not a mathematical upper bound."
